<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Compound proportion worker-hours</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A road crew of \({@w1@}\) workers, working \({@h1@}\) hours a day, takes \({@d1@}\) days to gravel a stretch of road.</p><p>(a) How many worker-hours does the job take?</p><p>[[input:ans1]] worker-hours [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) How many days would \({@w2@}\) workers take to do the same job, working \({@h2@}\) hours a day? Give your answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p>[[input:ans2]] days [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Reduce to one worker working one hour a day.</p><p>\({@w1@}\) workers working \({@h1@}\) hours a day take \({@d1@}\) days.<br/>1 worker working \({@h1@}\) hours a day takes \({@w1@} \times {@d1@} = {@w1*d1@}\) days.<br/>1 worker working 1 hour a day takes \({@h1@} \times {@w1*d1@} = {@ksh(W)@}\) days.</p><p>So the job is \({@w1@} \times {@h1@} \times {@d1@} = {@ksh(W)@}\) worker-hours.</p><p>(b) Change one quantity at a time and ask whether the answer gets bigger or smaller. More workers, and more hours a day, both mean fewer days.</p><p>\({@w2@}\) workers working \({@h2@}\) hours a day give \({@w2@} \times {@h2@} = {@w2*h2@}\) worker-hours a day.<br/>Days needed \(= {@ksh(W)@} \div {@w2*h2@} = {@dd(Dd)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
fr(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else sconcat("\\frac{", string(num(v)), "}{", string(denom(v)), "}");
r1(v) := floor(10*v+1/2)/10;
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: compound proportion with worker-hours. Source: original. [w1, h1, d1, w2, h2]: a road crew of w1 workers, h1 hours a day, d1 days; then w2 workers, h2 hours a day. Curated list, one seed per entry. */
L: [[14,9,8,16,7],[16,9,7,12,6],[24,7,6,14,9],[10,9,16,24,6],[16,9,20,18,10],[14,6,18,16,7],[18,6,11,8,9],[10,10,18,25,6],[30,7,15,14,10],[20,7,7,7,8]];
E: L[ix];
w1: E[1]; h1: E[2]; d1: E[3]; w2: E[4]; h2: E[5];
W: w1*h1*d1;
Dd: W/(w2*h2);
/* diagnostics */
one: w1*h1;
alldir: d1*w2*h2/(w1*h1);
wdir: d1*w2*h1/(w1*h2);
hdir: d1*w1*h2/(w2*h1);
noh: W/w2;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
